Implemented Vercel Web Analytics for the project

Changes made:
1. Installed @vercel/analytics package (version 2.0.1)
   - Added as a dependency in package.json
   - Updated pnpm-lock.yaml with the new package and its dependencies

2. Configured Analytics component in App.tsx
   - Imported { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/react'
   - Added <Analytics /> component to the application render tree
   - Placed inside the TooltipProvider for proper context integration

Implementation details:
- Framework: React + Vite
- Package Manager: pnpm
- Analytics Component: Follows official Vercel documentation for React/Vite applications
- The Analytics component is placed at the root level within the app providers to track all page views and interactions

Verification:
✓ Linting passed without errors (pnpm lint)
✓ Build completed successfully (pnpm build)
✓ All dependencies installed and lockfile updated
✓ No breaking changes to existing functionality

Next steps for the user:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard (Project Settings → Analytics)
3. After deployment, verify tracking by checking browser Network tab for /_vercel/insights/* requests

The Analytics component will automatically start collecting data once the application is deployed to Vercel with Analytics enabled in the dashboard.
